{"id": "EUVD-2026-107376", "enisaUuid": "70141ccb-436c-31e0-a2db-f1a4dd79e5b8", "description": "Multiple Cisco products are affected by a vulnerability in the Snort 3 Teredo Detection Engine that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart, resulting in an interruption of packet inspection.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to incomplete error checking when Snort 3 parses Teredo packets. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted Teredo packet to a targeted device to be parsed by Snort. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart unexpectedly, resulting in a DoS condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:12:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:11:21", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-misc-dos-6mB22qAK"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3wgh-x32w-jgcc", "CVE-2026-20197"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00405abd-4a11-3d56-b2e9-c14f803827a1", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.64.0"}, {"id": "012b9b18-2f0d-31e1-9950-3df0232d3d26", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.19.0"}, {"id": "016776aa-3076-3455-98d7-faa77de1ec5c", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.40.0"}, {"id": "0478b76a-9c49-3424-8334-06aa1d365cf6", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.43.0"}, {"id": "06f9ecdb-2029-31ac-85c6-397513566b04", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.4.4"}, {"id": "0b715873-2ca5-36d6-b01b-bf53d6f7c701", "produc